    {
      "id": "r20261031-a02",
      "title": "Why Handwriting Still Matters",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Today, most students type on laptops and phones. Some schools have even stopped teaching handwriting. But researchers say writing by hand is still an important skill.",
        "Studies show that students who take notes by hand remember more than those who type. The reason is simple: you cannot write as fast as you type, so you must choose the most important ideas and put them in your own words. This deeper thinking helps the brain learn. Writing by hand also uses more parts of the brain connected to memory and creativity.",
        "This does not mean we should throw away our keyboards. Typing is faster for long texts and easier to share. The smart approach is to use both: type when speed matters, and pick up a pen when you really need to learn and remember."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "handwriting": "tulisan tangan",
        "skill": "keterampilan",
        "take notes": "mencatat",
        "deeper": "lebih dalam",
        "creativity": "kreativitas",
        "approach": "pendekatan"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "Why do handwritten notes help memory?",
          "opts": [
